    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="0742" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1976</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 23, 1915, noon</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.15 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2617. Wolff’s Bureau sends out semi-officially notice that Germans working in
                    America on war material for Allies make themselves <pb facs="0743" n="485"
                        xml:id="pg485"/> liable to prosecution for treason as soon as they touch
                    German soil.</p>
                <p>The hate campaign against America continues with unabated violence, backed, I am
                    convinced, by Von Tirpitz, Reventlow and company, who seem to desire war
                    with America.</p>
                <p>Although I have advocated concessions to preserve peace, I am now convinced that
                    no concession that we make short of joining Germany in war will satisfy this
                    extreme party which seems for the present in control.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
